Consequences

Security Posture (Zero-Trust)

Non-Repudiation Guaranteed: Every API call routed to the upstream LLM is mathematically tied to a specific Workspace ID and validated client IP.

Zero Credential Usability Outside VPC: Stolen ciphertexts are completely inert; an attacker cannot utilize them without owning a valid running workspace, passing a strict SHA256 integrity check, and matching the dynamically anchored network location.

No Secret Sprawl: Static private keys are removed from the filesystem. The proxy uses temporary, auto-refreshing Vault tokens via IAM authentication.

Performance & Scalability

Extremely Low Overhead: For 99.9% of traffic, the proxy executes a simple lockless map check and string substitution. High-speed, non-blocking Go channels stream SSE payloads (chat typing effect) to the client with zero buffering delay.

Long Cache Lifespan (24 Hours): Since we explicitly handle real-time eviction through Coder lifecycle endpoints and self-heal after proxy crashes, a long-lived 24-hour cache TTL is safe, significantly reducing Vault and Coder API load.

Horizontal Scaling: The proxy is stateless across multiple pods. Multiple proxy replicas can run behind an AWS NLB because any pod can independently rehydrate any active session if a load balancer routes traffic to a replica missing the local cache entry.
